{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"124177","commit":"3ce442d80067f562ee0a097f52fa083828d3cd4d","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"Only `LP` and `OPENING_BRACKET` are handled. If ANTLR reports other tokens by symbol name in error messages (e.g. `RP`, `CLOSING_BRACKET`, or any future token), they will leak through. A more maintainable approach would be to build the replacement list from a single map (token-name → display-character) and iterate over it, so adding a new token is a one-line change rather than a new `Pattern` field plus a new `matcher`/`replaceAll` block.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java--5461:5547","promptId":"#27TGF","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5461,"endPos":5547,"startLine":136,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":136,"endLineOffset":94,"length":87}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java--5556:5665","promptId":"#6XMWW","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5556,"endPos":5665,"startLine":137,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":137,"endLineOffset":117,"length":110}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java-5557:5772-5940:6482","promptId":"#MJ3TG","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":5557,"endPos":5772,"startLine":144,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":147,"endLineOffset":13,"length":216}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5940,"endPos":6482,"startLine":148,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":158,"endLineOffset":13,"length":543}]}]},{"comment":"`BEFORE_REGEX`, `AFTER_REGEX`, `BEFORE_REPLACEMENT`, `AFTER_REPLACEMENT`, `REPLACE_LP`, and `REPLACE_LEFT_BRACKET` are all immutable and shared across instances. Declaring them `static final` (or moving them to a companion/constants class) makes the intent clearer and avoids re-creating the `Pattern` objects per parser instance.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java--5461:5547","promptId":"#27TGF","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5461,"endPos":5547,"startLine":136,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":136,"endLineOffset":94,"length":87}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java--5377:5452","promptId":"#K2SDV","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5377,"endPos":5452,"startLine":135,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":135,"endLineOffset":83,"length":76}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/EsqlParser.java--5291:5368","promptId":"#9J4